      "kind": "theorem",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.ConditionalScoreClosedDomain.conditional_score_closed_gradient_domain",
      "title": "Actual noncompact conditional scores in original closed gradient",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
          "label": "PBPS AppC1 authored original-gradient domain prerequisite",
          "scope": "Actual finite real Hilbert/Borel E including0. Fix actual finite mu and SAME original closable exact compact-C-infinity gradient D BEFORE ALL C1 f with actual MemLp f2mu and MemLp gradientf2mu. Genuine smooth cutoff exhaustion/derivative-product/weighted L2 limits put actual class pair into SAME closure graph, without compact support or extra spatial moment. Finite mu constants are genuinely in original closure domain with outputzero. For actual C1 Gibbs W/exp(-W) integrable, combine actual constants-domain with accepted one-way implication for full zero-output iff AEconstant on SAME D. Actual PBPS common Gaussian J/R/S/Sdensity/positive partitions/sourceC2 alpha beta eta cap and original D_y beforeALL constants/u/directions; real unnormalized y-score C1/L2/boundedgradient from accepted score producer transfers along ONLY explicit reflected density equality S2_y=S_y and enters SAME original closed graph. No R2=R or alternateD equality, global ordinary L1, C-infinity potential, gradient of rough representative, Nontrivial E, spatial moment, supplied domain/fullkernel/spectralgap/Poincare certificate, epsilon0/range/centering/measurablejointselector/core/BL/main/composition. TV never transfers unbounded cost."
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        "lake build Tests.WeightedC1GradientDomain"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "Full finite real Hilbert/Borel E including0; source V C2 and NNReal0<alpha<=beta with true all-point/all-vector alphaI<=HessV<=betaI, eta>0 and beta*eta<=1.",
        "Actual common Gaussian J=(x,x+sqrteta*xi)#(mu*standardGaussian), Markov/disintegrating R and reflected S_y=(2x-y)#R_y; actual W_y(z)=V((y+z)/2)+norm(z-y)^2/(8eta), S_y=volume.tilted(-W_y), integrable/positive partition. SAME dense closable exact original D_y precedes ALL constants/domain elements/directions.",
        "Actual unnormalized parameter-y score s_y(u)[a]=-DV((y+u)/2)[a]/2-inner(y-u,a)/(4eta), not the negative u-gradient or already centered normalized score. Its C1/scalarL2/boundedgradient is produced by the accepted score theorem; only literal S2_y=S_y from exact density is used."
      ],
      "statement": "Construct true common conditional J/R/S, positive reflected C2 potential and SAME original D_y before ALL c/u/a. Produce actual constant domain, full kernel equality and actual noncompact unnormalized directional-y score C1/gradient bound with true scalar/vector L2 class pair in SAME D_y.closure.graph. No R2/R identity or alternate operator is assumed.",
      "formula": "s_y(u)[a]=-\\tfrac12DV((y+u)/2)[a]-\\langle y-u,a\\rangle/(4\\eta),\\quad([s_y[a]],[\\nabla s_y[a]])\\in\\operatorname{graph}\\overline D_y,\\quad\\|\\nabla s_y[a]\\|\\le(\\eta^{-1}-\\alpha)\\|a\\|/4.",
      "boundary": "Actual finite real Hilbert/Borel E including0. Fix actual finite mu and SAME original closable exact compact-C-infinity gradient D BEFORE ALL C1 f with actual MemLp f2mu and MemLp gradientf2mu. Genuine smooth cutoff exhaustion/derivative-product/weighted L2 limits put actual class pair into SAME closure graph, without compact support or extra spatial moment. Finite mu constants are genuinely in original closure domain with outputzero. For actual C1 Gibbs W/exp(-W) integrable, combine actual constants-domain with accepted one-way implication for full zero-output iff AEconstant on SAME D. Actual PBPS common Gaussian J/R/S/Sdensity/positive partitions/sourceC2 alpha beta eta cap and original D_y beforeALL constants/u/directions; real unnormalized y-score C1/L2/boundedgradient from accepted score producer transfers along ONLY explicit reflected density equality S2_y=S_y and enters SAME original closed graph. No R2=R or alternateD equality, global ordinary L1, C-infinity potential, gradient of rough representative, Nontrivial E, spatial moment, supplied domain/fullkernel/spectralgap/Poincare certificate, epsilon0/range/centering/measurablejointselector/core/BL/main/composition. TV never transfers unbounded cost.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Produce actual common law and original operator before all queries",
          "text": "Use the accepted conditional gradient-zero producer for common Gaussian augmentation, disintegration/reflection, actual W_y/density/positive partition and SAME original dense/closable/exact D_y. No new operator is chosen for a constant, u or direction.",
          "formula": "S_y=(2x-y)_\\#R_y=Z_y^{-1}e^{-W_y}du,\\quad W_y(u)=V((y+u)/2)+\\|u-y\\|^2/(8\\eta).",
          "lean": "ConditionalGradientKernel.conditional_gradient_zero_ae_constant"
        },
        {
          "title": "Produce true constants-domain and kernel on this SAME law",
          "text": "Apply the new shared constant-domain and Gibbs kernel equality leaves to the actual S_y and SAME D_y. Source C2 W_y yields C1; the actual partition and exact density feed the Gibbs leaf.",
          "formula": "\\forall c\\ \\exists u\\in\\operatorname{dom}\\overline D_y:\\ u=c,\\ \\overline D_yu=0;\\quad\\overline D_yu=0\\iff u\\text{ is AE constant}.",
          "lean": "WeightedC1GradientDomain.constants_in_closed_gradient; GibbsGradientKernelEquality.closed_gradient_zero_iff_ae_constant"
        },
        {
          "title": "Transfer actual score data along literal normalized density equality",
          "text": "The accepted score producer gives auxiliary S2_y with exactly the same explicit normalized reflected density, actual C1 scalar score/L2 and sharp gradient bound. Prove S2_y=S_y only through that density and rewrite scalar MemLp; do not identify auxiliary R2/R or separately chosen conditional versions globally.",
          "formula": "S_{2,y}=\\operatorname{tilted}(-W_y)=S_y,\\quad\\|\\nabla s_y[a]\\|\\le(\\eta^{-1}-\\alpha)\\|a\\|/4.",
          "lean": "ConditionalScoreDomain.conditional_curvature_and_score_domain; conditional_score_closed_gradient_domain"
        },
        {
          "title": "Produce genuine score gradient L2 and its original graph pair",
          "text": "Actual C1 score gives continuous genuine gradient, whose pointwise bound and actual Markov finite probability give vector MemLp. The new weighted C1 producer puts scalar/vector classes into SAME original D_y.closure.graph. True nonquadratic eta1/2 and E0 constant7 tests exercise source domain/kernel results; no Poincare is asserted.",
          "formula": "([s_y[a]],[\\nabla s_y[a]])\\in\\operatorname{graph}\\overline D_y.",
          "lean": "MemLp.of_bound; WeightedC1GradientDomain.c1_in_closed_gradient; Tests.WeightedC1GradientDomain.actual_nonquadratic_score_original_domain"
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "Construct true common conditional J/R/S, positive reflected C2 potential and SAME original D_y before ALL c/u/a. Produce actual constant domain, full kernel equality and actual noncompact unnormalized directional-y score C1/gradient bound with true scalar/vector L2 class pair in SAME D_y.closure.graph. No R2/R identity or alternate operator is assumed.",
      "lean_proof": "Produce actual common law and original operator before all queries; Produce true constants-domain and kernel on this SAME law; Transfer actual score data along literal normalized density equality; Produce genuine score gradient L2 and its original graph pair",
      "astis_dependencies": [
        "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.WeightedC1GradientDomain.c1_in_closed_gradient",
